{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>A fitting man.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: איש — even a layman; עתי — even in impurity, meaning that if he became impure he enters the courtyard and sends it off. עתי — even on the Sabbath, meaning that if the goat took ill he carries it on his shoulder on the Sabbath and goes, and needless to say if it did not take ill, that it carries itself; but even if it took ill, which is like something tied and like a burden — even so it is permitted to set it upon his shoulder on the Sabbath. And this is the meaning of עתי — even on the Sabbath."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:02.106640753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}